        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_eedea83e00c640ca9b1e7fca6b6820bb",
      "statement": "The Error schema (openapi/components/schemas/Error.yaml) requires kind (always 'Error'), code (machine-readable), and reason (human-readable); handlers.APIHandler.respondError and the unexported auth.respondError (used by authn/authz middleware) both build this exact shape, each deriving code as 'HTTP_<status>' rather than the semantic codes shown in the spec's own examples.",
      "evidence": [
